=== p2-windows · W7 · page:system/Help (WinUI 3 / Fluent) ===
Parity unit : page:system/Help   kind=page   web route=(unrouted)
Web source  : web/src/features/system/pages/HelpPage.tsx
ADR refs    : ADR-002, ADR-004, ADR-005, ADR-006, ADR-011, ADR-013, ADR-014, ADR-015
Runner      : .NET 10.0.300 SDK present (dotnet --version 10.0.300) — NOT blocked.

=== APPROACH ===
- The repository's WinUI app is code-first C# (no .xaml page files); every feature surface lives under
  apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/feature-views/<Name>/ as <Name>.Model.cs (pure, Microsoft.UI-free projection,
  unit-tested headlessly), an optional <Name>.Source.cs (the generated-client feed) and <Name>.ViewModel.cs
  (INotifyPropertyChanged state holder), plus <Name>.cs (the Fluent view), exactly as the sibling W7
  OnboardingPage / ApiLogsPage / ReferenceLinksSection do. The generated prompt's idealized
  "TeslaSync/Features/System/HelpPage.xaml + HelpPageViewModel.cs" is mapped onto these real conventions. The
  namespace is TeslaSync.App.FeatureViews.SystemOps (NOT ...System — a `.System` sub-namespace shadows the global
  System namespace and breaks unqualified System.* references; SystemOps also aligns with RouteGroup.SystemOps,
  the manifest's system/ group).
- Data binding (ADR-004): the manifest declares NO API data sources — the web page renders from navigation params
  / local state only (it binds just useTranslation + usePageTitle and maps a static, intentionally short curated
  HELP_LINKS catalog). So there is no generated-client feed and no <Name>.Source.cs; HelpPageViewModel projects
  the static HelpLinkCatalog through HelpProjection with zero HTTP. LoadAsync/RefreshAsync honour the page
  lifecycle (OnLoaded → LoadAsync) by re-projecting synchronously (no fabricated network call).
- One data state (manifest: success): the web page has no fetch/loading/error branch, so the honest native union
  is HelpState.Success (the curated catalog yielded links → intro panel + card grid) plus a defensive
  HelpState.Empty branch (a null/empty catalog → the intro panel + a friendly TsEmptyState, never a blank region,
  ADR-011). The intro GlassPanel is always visible.
- Panels (ADR-005): GlassPanel1 = the framing intro paragraph (web help.intro) inside a TsGlassPanel (Mica/glass
  via the W1 surface tokens); GlassPanel2 = the curated link card — one TsGlassPanel per HELP_LINKS entry, laid
  out in a responsive 1/2/3-column grid (web grid sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3, breakpoints 640/1024) that
  recomputes on SizeChanged. Each card wraps a chromeless HyperlinkButton (accent icon tile + PanelTitle-weight
  title + secondary description + trailing chevron) whose Click raises NavigationRequested with the web `to`
  route. No hardcoded colours/typography — DisplayTokens (TsColor*/TsRadius* + the cyan accent token) drive
  light/dark/high-contrast from W1.
- Navigation entry: the web HelpPage is unrouted in App.tsx (the component exists + is unit-tested
  TestRagHelpAIOffHidesAssistantAndDocsLinksWork, but is not wired into a visible nav route). Per the prompt's
  "(if routed) map (unrouted) to it as a deep link", the Windows shell exposes it as a HIDDEN deep-link:
  RouteTable.cs adds Hidden("Help","help",RouteGroup.SystemOps,"Help") (ShowInNav=false — not in the nav pane,
  matching the web's not-in-nav status) and ShellWindow.xaml.cs registers the factory
  (new FeatureViews.SystemOps.HelpPage(); NavigationRequested → NavigateTo). The five curated cards navigate to
  existing canonical routes already in RouteTable (docs/status-api, onboarding, system-status, search, chatbot) —
  this page introduces NO new surface (web ADR-015 §I3 baseline-intact). NavigationTests stays green (the Hidden,
  non-parameterised SystemOps route does not affect the single-catch-all, group-coverage or navigable-route
  assertions).
- The AIRAGHelp AI surface the web page renders alongside the baseline is a separate, conditional component
  (web @/components/ai/AIRAGHelp, hidden when ai_mode='off' per ADR-015 §I5) with its own parity unit; it is not
  part of page:system/Help's manifest record (no data source / panel / string for it) and is out of scope here.
- SI units N/A (this surface has no unit-bearing fields — only static link copy); no charts, no maps; no SSE/live
  source and therefore no >2-min staleness pill (ADR-013 N/A).
- i18n (ADR-014): every visible literal resolves through the ILocalizer facade with the web key names + English
  defaults. help.title + help.intro + the ten help.baseline.links.* card keys are already present verbatim
  (web key names) in Strings/en/Resources.resw as translation.help.* with the web English values; no catalog edit
  was needed. The defensive empty message routes through localizer.GetString("help.empty", …) (fallback only;
  never a hardcoded literal). RecordingLocalizer asserts every key flows through the facade.
- a11y (ADR-015): GlassPanel1 carries AutomationProperties.Name; the link region is a Navigation landmark; each
  card's HyperlinkButton carries its composed Narrator name (title + description) and is keyboard- + pointer-
  invokable at ≥40px target size; decorative icon tiles / chevrons are AccessibilityView.Raw; the page exposes a
  Group automation peer; DisplayTokens drive light/dark + high-contrast.

